# DORMANT — NOT the filter for the production image. Docker reads the .dockerignore at
# the root of the BUILD CONTEXT, and the context is now the repo root (render.yaml:
# `dockerContext: .`), so the file that governs the Render build is ../.dockerignore.
# It moved because frames/ lives beside server/ and a ./server context could not reach
# it, leaving the image with zero frame packs.
#
# This file is kept only so that an ad-hoc `docker build ./server` (or any tool that
# still treats server/ as the context) does not sweep node_modules and secrets into a
# tarball. Anything added here must be added to ../.dockerignore as well — that is the
# one that decides what production ships.
node_modules
jobs
jobs.json
public/videos
public/dist
uploads
asset_cache
asset_library
scrub
framecheck/occ_test
showcase
*.log
.env
config.json
.git
